{
  "_how_to": [
    "This file is the gallery. Each entry below is one artwork, shown in this order.",
    "",
    "1. Put the files in public/artwork/   images: jpg, jpeg, png, webp   videos: mp4, mov, webm",
    "2. Add an entry here listing them. That is all that is required.",
    "",
    "files        the filenames inside public/artwork/, in the order to show them.        (required)",
    "             The FIRST one is what appears in the grid — a still, or a video that loops there.",
    "             Everything after it (more photos, a video) shows when the work is opened.",
    "title        shown on the pointer when hovering, and in the lightbox                   (required)",
    "description  a line or two, shown in the lightbox under the title                      (optional)",
    "size         the physical size as you would write it, e.g. \"60 × 80 cm\"             (optional)",
    "year         a number, shown after the title                                            (optional)",
    "type         \"painting\" or \"animation\", for the filter. Left out, anything with a video",
    "             counts as an animation and everything else as a painting.                (optional)",
    "",
    "Sizes are read from the files themselves when the site builds — never type them.",
    "For video prefer .mp4 (H.264): it carries its size and plays everywhere. .mov is fine too;",
    ".webm cannot be measured here and is laid out 16:9. A .mov straight off an iPhone (HEVC) may not play in Chrome.",
    "An entry whose files cannot be found is skipped with a warning in the build log, never an error."
  ],
